beginMessage / sendFragment / endMessage, with a ping in between:
  frame: opcode  1  fin=0  payload 5
  frame: opcode  9  fin=1  payload 0
  frame: opcode  0  fin=0  payload 2
  frame: opcode  0  fin=0  payload 5
  frame: opcode  0  fin=1  payload 0
the client's takeMessage: "Hello, world" (one message, 12 bytes)
setFragmentSize(4) cuts every message into frames of at most 4 bytes:
  frame: opcode  1  fin=0  payload 4
  frame: opcode  0  fin=0  payload 4
  frame: opcode  0  fin=1  payload 2
a stream handler gets the pieces and keeps nothing:
  frame: opcode  2  fin=0  payload 3
  frame: opcode  0  fin=0  payload 5
  frame: opcode  0  fin=1  payload 0
  piece of 3 bytes, flags 1: "abc"
  piece of 5 bytes, flags 0: "defgh"
  piece of 0 bytes, flags 2: ""
takeMessage afterwards: null
